Subject: rpmalloc: Bound per-thread reservations on Windows ARM64 hosts

Wine ARM64 can run with a 39-bit user address space. A 256 MiB span plus
alignment reserves 512 MiB for each thread's size-class heap, exhausting
that space in applications with hundreds of threads. A 64 MiB span still
contains the largest allocator page and does not change allocation limits.
Keep the native Linux allocator configuration unchanged.

--- a/External/rpmalloc/rpmalloc/rpmalloc.c
+++ b/External/rpmalloc/rpmalloc/rpmalloc.c
@@ -188,1 +188,7 @@
+#if PLATFORM_WINDOWS
+/* Wine ARM64 hosts may have only 39 bits of user virtual address space.
+ * Keep one large page per span rather than reserving four per thread. */
+#define SPAN_SIZE LARGE_PAGE_SIZE
+#else
 #define SPAN_SIZE (256 * 1024 * 1024)
+#endif
